parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>280</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 320 right parenthesis degree plus left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 320 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 18 x plus 640 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>640</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 9 x minus 140 right parenthesis degree plus left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 320 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180 period degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math> Of the given choices, only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 18 x plus 280 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>280</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math> is not equivalent to any of these expressions and could not be the sum of the measures of any two of the angles.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of two angles that are adjacent to the given angle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the sum of the measure of the given angle and the measure of its opposite angle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measure of the given angle and the measure of an angle adjacent to the given angle.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727993,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"c41eb616","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1776362727993,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"8f2e34ca-40c9-466a-beaf-7b8cda35144d","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"6b8c0622-c498-4029-a61f-ad16c2bfea44","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Two lines intersect at exactly one point, forming two acute angles and two obtuse angles. The measure of one of these angles is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 9 x minus 140 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>140</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Which of the following could <strong>NOT</strong> be the sum of the measures of any two of these angles?</p>","keys":["448a85c0-3803-4780-8417-0ed0e0cd3c95"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"448a85c0-3803-4780-8417-0ed0e0cd3c95","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 18 x plus 280 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>280</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"8d0e847d-a811-44ba-abe6-a98af0d40477","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 18 x plus 640 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>640</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"da9fed5d-099c-4516-93bc-0bc5e4a0310e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 18 x minus 280 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>280</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"da9586ef-50a0-4ba1-b160-e42b34e61a57","