"><mo>(</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>280</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 320 right parenthesis degree plus left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 320 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 18 x plus 640 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>640</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 9 x minus 140 right parenthesis degree plus left parenthesis minus 9 x plus 320 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>320</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180 period degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math> Of the given choices, only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis minus 18 x plus 280 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>280</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math> is not equivalent to any of these expressions and could not be the sum of the measures of any two of the angles.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of two angles that are adjacent to the given angle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the sum of the measure of the given angle and the measure of its opposite angle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measure of the given angle and the measure of an angle adjacent to the given angle.</p>","externalid":"8f2e34ca-40c9-466a-beaf-7b8cda35144d","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1776362727993,"updateDate":1776362727993}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727993, 1776362727993),
    ($SATQ$c447367f$SATQ$, $SATQ$a8c9a7ac-0d28-45aa-b013-1691f98acb24$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane has its center at <math alttext="left parenthesis 19 comma 18 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and has a radius of <math alttext="9 k"><mrow>
	<mn>9</mn>
	<mi>k</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Which equation represents this circle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a123bafd-05f1-4f2f-a336-98a1042743e0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 81 k\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>81</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"2835ce8d-7ea4-45a9-9c21-124c0f982c59","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 81 k squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>81</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"22a2f92d-a9b4-4c14-9f76-fd86b25621c5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 9 k\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"5559405d-6f5c-4d1b-b558-9200e4ae5a38","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 9 k squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2835ce8d-7ea4-45a9-9c21-124c0f982c59"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The equation of a circle in the <em>x</em><em>y</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>. It’s given that this circle has a center at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 19 comma 18 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and a radius of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 k"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="18"><mn>18</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 k"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals left parenthesis 9 k right parenthesis squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 81 k squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the equation that represents this circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 81 k squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 StartRoot k EndRoot"><mn>9</mn><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 k"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 9 k EndRoot"><msqrt><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></msqrt></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 k"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>
