alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 19 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 18 right parenthesis squared equals 81 k squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 StartRoot k EndRoot\"><mn>9</mn><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 k\"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot 9 k EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></msqrt></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 k\"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot 9 EndRoot k\"><msqrt><mn>9</mn></msqrt><mi>k</mi></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 k\"><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>","externalid":"a8c9a7ac-0d28-45aa-b013-1691f98acb24","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1776362727993,"updateDate":1776362727993}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727993, 1776362727993),
    ($SATQ$c4e5e23c$SATQ$, $SATQ$0103767c-8ef7-4ec8-a9fb-3a3fa9a5469f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The length of one side of square M is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> times the length of one side of square N. The area of square N is <math alttext="49"><mn>49</mn>
</math> square feet. What is the area, in square feet, of square M?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5da8d609-87eb-47af-8036-37d1d9bdaab6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,764\"><mn>1,764</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"70e562c6-5442-4464-8ec4-d881e9e4bc18","content":"<p><math alttext=\"504\"><mn>504</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"40ee4feb-8c76-4c72-a5c2-b3a72235a8ca","content":"<p><math alttext=\"294\"><mn>294</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"eb9130d7-c7b3-4eae-807c-27e511147c38","content":"<p><math alttext=\"252\"><mn>252</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5da8d609-87eb-47af-8036-37d1d9bdaab6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The area,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a square is given by the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals s squared"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math> is the length of one side of the square. Let <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> represent the length, in feet, of one side of square N. It's given that the area of square N is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="49"><mn>49</mn></math> square feet; therefore, it follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="49 equals x squared"><mn>49</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the length of one side of square M is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6"><mn>6</mn></math> times the length of one side of square N. Therefore, the length of one side of square M can be represented by the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6 x"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6 x"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals s squared"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis 6 x right parenthesis squared"><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 36 x squared"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Since <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="49 equals x squared"><mn>49</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="49"><mn>49</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x squared"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> in the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 36 x squared"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 36 left parenthesis 49 right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 1,764"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,764</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square feet, of square M is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,764"><mn>1,764</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
