s squared\"><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 36 x squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"49 equals x squared\"><mn>49</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 36 x squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 36 left parenthesis 49 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 1,764\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,764</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square feet, of square M is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1,764\"><mn>1,764</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"0103767c-8ef7-4ec8-a9fb-3a3fa9a5469f","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1776362727991,"updateDate":1776362727991}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727991, 1776362727991),
    ($SATQ$c6dff223$SATQ$, $SATQ$2ec14ac8-bf5b-46cc-8993-b907b006b31c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Right triangles and trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Triangle&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is similar to triangle&nbsp;<math alttext="upper D upper E upper F"><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></math>, where angle <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
