$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The circle above has center <span class="italic">O</span>, the length of arc <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_005_5ed113a8.png" alt="A, D C"></span></span> is <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_006_20938941.png" alt="5 pi"></span></span>, and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_007_f0beae7c.png" alt="x equals 100"></span></span>. What is the length of arc <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_008_4b9add73.png" alt="A, B C"></span></span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_000_574ccba3.png\" alt=\"9 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_001_bb1bd172.png\" alt=\"13 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_002_5285ce71.png\" alt=\"18 pi\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_003_12ccc3c3.png\" alt=\"13 halves pi\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The ratio of the lengths of two arcs of a circle is equal to the ratio of the measures of the central angles that subtend the arcs. It&rsquo;s given that arc <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_009_8aca49b6.png" alt="A D C"></span> is subtended by a central angle with measure 100&deg;. Since the sum of the measures of the angles about a point is 360&deg;, it follows that arc <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_010_93b33b38.png" alt="A B C"></span> is subtended by a central angle with measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_011_f4e76874.png" alt="360 degrees minus 100 degrees, equals 260 degrees"></span>. If <span class="italic">s</span> is the length of arc <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_012_93b33b38.png" alt="A B C"></span>, then <span class="italic">s</span> must satisfy the ratio <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_013_fa72d624.png" alt="the fraction s over 5 pi, end fraction equals, the fraction 260 over 100"></span>. Reducing the fraction <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_014_ba6459ab.png" alt="260 over 100"></span> to its simplest form gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_015_878ae7d9.png" alt="the fraction 13 over 5"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_016_2418738d.png" alt="the fraction s over 5 pi, end fraction, equals, the fraction 13 over 5"></span>. Multiplying both sides of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_017_2418738d.png" alt="the fraction s over 5 pi, end fraction, equals, the fraction 13 over 5"></span> by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_018_08e0281f.png" alt="5 pi"></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_019_0d9cb012.png" alt="s equals 13 pi"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the length of an arc consisting of exactly half of the circle, but arc <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_020_93b33b38.png" alt="A B C"></span> is greater than half of the circle. Choice C is incorrect. This is the total circumference of the circle. Choice D is incorrect. This is half the length of arc <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8345903/img_021_93b33b38.png" alt="A B C"></span>, not its full length.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
