</math>. What is the perimeter of the rectangle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5903e5db-bcdb-4112-a6cb-5ad3425ea7b9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"73d6067a-be76-4f42-943b-bab84fdb800b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"26\"><mn>26</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"81fbedac-9925-4517-b779-b419ad712818","content":"<p><math alttext=\"38\"><mn>38</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5abbb3c0-b11b-4ff0-a31b-e0be3b11978b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"52\"><mn>52</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["81fbedac-9925-4517-b779-b419ad712818"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The perimeter of a quadrilateral is the sum of the lengths of its four sides. It's given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> and a width of <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>. It follows that the rectangle has two sides with length <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> and two sides with length <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the perimeter of the rectangle is <math alttext="13 plus 13 plus 6 plus 6"><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, or <math alttext="38"><mn>38</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum of the lengths of the two sides with length <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>, not the sum of the lengths of all four sides of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the sum of the lengths of the two sides with length <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math>, not the sum of the lengths of all four sides of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the perimeter of a rectangle that has four sides with length <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math>, not two sides with length <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> and two sides with length <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c88183f7","external_id":"60500dd8-893a-4fea-903d-de896120774c","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"98ae7657-0726-41ff-bb2a-f6df51755a8e","uId":"910025c6-1c1b-4048-bab2-d566dcf2bd01","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math> and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. What is the perimeter of the rectangle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5903e5db-bcdb-4112-a6cb-5ad3425ea7b9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"73d6067a-be76-4f42-943b-bab84fdb800b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"26\"><mn>26</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"81fbedac-9925-4517-b779-b419ad712818","content":"<p><math alttext=\"38\"><mn>38</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5abbb3c0-b11b-4ff0-a31b-e0be3b11978b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"52\"><mn>52</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["81fbedac-9925-4517-b779-b419ad712818"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The perimeter of a quadrilateral is the sum of the lengths of its four sides. It's given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math> and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. It follows that the rectangle has two sides with length <math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math> and two sides with length <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, the perimeter of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"13 plus 13 plus 6 plus 6\"><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"38\"><mn>38</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. 