$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In the given triangle, <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_001_cd5bf285.png" alt="the length of side A, B equals the length of side A, C "></span></span> and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_002_006f80b2.png" alt="angle A, B C "></span></span> has a measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_003_b63085cb.png" alt="67 degrees"></span>. What is the value of <span class="italic">x</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">36</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">46</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">58</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">70</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_004_cd5bf285.png" alt="the length of A, B equals the length of A, C"></span>, the measures of their corresponding angles, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_005_006f80b2.png" alt="angle A, B C "></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_006_1131c684.png" alt="angle A, C B"></span>, are equal. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_007_006f80b2.png" alt="angle A, B C "></span> has a measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_008_b63085cb.png" alt="67 degrees"></span>, the measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_009_1131c684.png" alt="angle A, C B"></span> is also <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_010_b63085cb.png" alt="67 degrees"></span>. Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles in a triangle is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_011_429202ed.png" alt="180 degrees"></span>, it follows that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_012_f91be4d0.png" alt="67 plus 67, plus x, equals 180"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_013_0ada05f0.png" alt="134 plus x, equals 180"></span>. Subtracting by 134 on both sides of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_014_2319edd3.png" alt="x equals 46"></span>.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from calculation errors.</p></p>
