th-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_011_429202ed.png\" alt=\"180 degrees\"></span>, it follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_012_f91be4d0.png\" alt=\"67 plus 67, plus x, equals 180\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_013_0ada05f0.png\" alt=\"134 plus x, equals 180\"></span>. Subtracting by 134 on both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c8d60e48/img_014_2319edd3.png\" alt=\"x equals 46\"></span>.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from calculation errors.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":15,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959621,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"c8d60e48","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959621,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"026874-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"111b9e49-eab3-456b-8179-7e6b6929106e","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"026874-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents triangle B A, C, such that side B C is horizontal and vertex A, is above side B C. Angle A, is labeled x degrees.\" width=\"89\" height=\"101\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the given triangle, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side A, B equals the length of side A, C \"></span></span> and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle A, B C \"></span></span> has a measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"67 degrees\"></span>. What is the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">36</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">46</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">58</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">70</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of A, B equals the length of A, C\"></span>, the measures of their corresponding angles, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle A, B C \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle A, C B\"></span>, are equal. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle A, B C \"></span> has a measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"67 degrees\"></span>, the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle A, C B\"></span> is also <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"67 degrees\"></span>. Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles in a triangle is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees\"></span>, it follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"67 plus 67, plus x, equals 180\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"134 plus x, equals 180\"></span>. Subtracting by 134 on both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 46\"></span>.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from calculation errors.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959621,"updateDate":1691007959621}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959621, 1691007959621),
