</math> inches, which of the following is closest to the volume, in cubic inches, of this hemisphere?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e09fc2a3-e3b9-421c-9a18-9146403129b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,500\"><mn>1,500</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"357cdf3c-fe88-4f72-a5ff-e8d7e4502edd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6,100\"><mn>6,100</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"6c7fd39c-b36c-4aab-9d1f-35d9cf46c1d3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"30,900\"><mn>30,900</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e14cf156-7596-4c80-a048-c57883901437","content":"<p><math alttext=\"41,200\"><mn>41,200</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e14cf156-7596-4c80-a048-c57883901437"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The volume, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a sphere is given by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals four thirds pi r cubed"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the sphere. Since a hemisphere is half of a sphere, it follows that the volume, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a hemisphere is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis four thirds right parenthesis pi r cubed"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals two thirds pi r cubed"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="27"><mn>27</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in this formula yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals two thirds pi left parenthesis 27 right parenthesis cubed"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, which gives&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals 13,122 pi"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13,122</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;is approximately equal to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="41,223.98"><mn>41,223.98</mn></math>. Therefore, the choice that is closest to the volume, in cubic inches, of this hemisphere is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="41,200"><mn>41,200</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c984f1a5","external_id":"5b086c61-e308-4d87-b595-7b21a6d05163","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d9cb19da-b8a1-4a38-904b-6d3edde56460","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>A hemisphere is half of a sphere. If a hemisphere has a radius of <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math> inches, which of the following is closest to the volume, in cubic inches, of this hemisphere?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e09fc2a3-e3b9-421c-9a18-9146403129b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,500\"><mn>1,500</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"357cdf3c-fe88-4f72-a5ff-e8d7e4502edd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6,100\"><mn>6,100</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"6c7fd39c-b36c-4aab-9d1f-35d9cf46c1d3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"30,900\"><mn>30,900</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e14cf156-7596-4c80-a048-c57883901437","content":"<p><math alttext=\"41,200\"><mn>41,200</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["e14cf156-7596-4c80-a048-c57883901437"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a sphere is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals four thirds pi r cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the sphere. Since a hemisphere is half of a sphere, it follows that the volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a hemisphere is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis four thirds right parenthesis pi r cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals two thirds pi r cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in this formula yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals two thirds pi left parenthesis 27 right parenthesis cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, which gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals 13,122 pi\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13,122</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;is approximately equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"41,223.98\"><mn>41,223.98</mn></math>. Therefore, the choice that is closest to the volume, in cubic inches, of this hemisphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"41,200\"><mn>41,200</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017718,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"c984f1a5","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1755117017718,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"5b086c61-e308-4d87-b595-7b21a6d05163","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"d9cb19da-b8a1-4a38-904b-6d3edde56460","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p>A hemisphere is half of a sphere. If a hemisphere has a radius of <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math> inches, which of the following is closest to the volume, in cubic inches, of this hemisphere?</p>","keys":["e14cf156-7596-4c80-a048-c57883901437"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"e09fc2a3-e3b9-421c-9a18-9146403129b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,500\"><mn>1,500</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"357cdf3c-fe88-4f72-a5ff-e8d7e4502edd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6,100\"><mn>6,100</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"6c7fd39c-b36c-4aab-9d1f-35d9cf46c1d3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"30,900\"><mn>30,900</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e14cf156-7596-4c80-a048-c57883901437","content":"<p><math alttext=\"41,200\"><mn>41,200</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a sphere is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals four thirds pi r cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the sphere. Since a hemisphere is half of a sphere, it follows that the volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a hemisphere is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis four thirds right parenthesis pi r cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals two thirds pi r cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in this formula yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals two thirds pi left parenthesis 27 right parenthesis cubed\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>27</mn></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, which gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals 13,122 pi\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13,122</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;is approximately equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"41,223.98\"><mn>41,223.98</mn></math>. Therefore, the choice that is closest to the volume, in cubic inches, of this hemisphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"41,200\"><mn>41,200</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"5b086c61-e308-4d87-b595-7b21a6d05163","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017718,"updateDate":1755117017718}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017718, 1755117017718),
    ($SATQ$c9931030$SATQ$, $SATQ$84b26634-2244-45e6-8504-ea367a0f2049$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$665adb83-0ed4-4f1b-baa1-36b2ef92be0d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Right triangles and trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="upper R upper S equals 20"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="upper S upper T equals 48"><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="upper T upper R equals 52"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn>
</math></p>
<p>The side lengths of right triangle <math alttext="upper R upper S upper T"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> are given. Triangle <math alttext="upper R upper S upper T"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math alttext="upper U upper V upper W"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>W</mi></math>, where <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math> corresponds to <math alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> corresponds to <math alttext="upper W"><mi>W</mi>
</math>. What is the value of <math alttext="tangent upper W"><mi>tan</mi><mi>W</mi></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"92a1ef8c-7060-4466-9fa8-27745e2ac4d6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five thirteenths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>13</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c0c083ab-909a-4509-88ee-1af9eb74d842","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"88bcfe4f-3189-4a98-a4ec-c6800552f4cd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over 13 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mn>13</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0c808f5b-778e-4d22-a84f-b4eff8b1d39c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c0c083ab-909a-4509-88ee-1af9eb74d842"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It's given that right triangle <math alttext="upper R upper S upper T"><mrow>
	<mi>R</mi>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext="upper U upper V upper W"><mrow>
	<mi>U</mi>
	<mi>V</mi>
	<mi>W</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math> corresponds to <math alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> corresponds to <math alttext="upper W"><mi>W</mi>
</math>. It's given that the side lengths of the right triangle <math alttext="upper R upper S upper T"><mrow>
	<mi>R</mi>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
</mrow>
</math> are <math alttext="upper R upper S equals 20"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>R</mi>
		<mi>S</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>20</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, <math alttext="upper S upper T equals 48"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>S</mi>
		<mi>T</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>48</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext="upper T upper R equals 52"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn></math>. Corresponding angles in similar triangles are equal. It follows that the measure of angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext="upper W"><mi>W</mi>
</math>.&nbsp;The hypotenuse of a right triangle is the longest side. It follows that the hypotenuse of triangle&nbsp;<math alttext="upper R upper S upper T"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is side <math alttext="upper T upper R"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. The hypotenuse of a right triangle is the side opposite the right angle. Therefore, angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math> is a right angle. The adjacent side of an acute angle in a right triangle is the side closest to the angle that is not the hypotenuse. It follows that the adjacent side of angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> is side <math alttext="upper S upper T"><mrow>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. The opposite side of an acute angle in a right triangle is the side across from the acute angle. It follows that the opposite side of angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> is side <math alttext="upper R upper S"><mrow>
	<mi>R</mi>
	<mi>S</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. The tangent of an acute angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side. Therefore, <math alttext="tangent upper T equals StartFraction upper R upper S Over upper S upper T EndFraction"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math alttext="20"><mn>20</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="upper R upper S"><mrow>
	<mi>R</mi>
	<mi>S</mi>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="48"><mn>48</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="upper S upper T"><mrow>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
</mrow>
</math> in this equation yields <math alttext="tangent upper T equals StartFraction 20 Over 48 EndFraction"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>48</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="tangent upper T equals five twelfths"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>. The tangents of two acute angles with equal measures are equal. Since the measure of angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext="upper W"><mi>W</mi>
</math>, it follows that <math alttext="tangent upper T equals tangent upper W"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext="five twelfths"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext="tangent upper T"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi></math> in this equation yields <math alttext="five twelfths equals tangent upper W"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="tangent upper W"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math> is <math alttext="five twelfths"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="sine upper W"><mi>sin</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="cosine upper W"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="StartFraction 1 Over tangent upper W EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c9931030","external_id":"84b26634-2244-45e6-8504-ea367a0f2049","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"665adb83-0ed4-4f1b-baa1-36b2ef92be0d","uId":"8c9abab8-de69-4713-93d3-c72423171dc9","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"upper R upper S equals 20\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"upper S upper T equals 48\"><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"upper T upper R equals 52\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p>The side lengths of right triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> are given. Triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper W\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>W</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"tangent upper W\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>W</mi></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"92a1ef8c-7060-4466-9fa8-27745e2ac4d6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five thirteenths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>13</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c0c083ab-909a-4509-88ee-1af9eb74d842","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"88bcfe4f-3189-4a98-a4ec-c6800552f4cd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over 13 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mn>13</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0c808f5b-778e-4d22-a84f-b4eff8b1d39c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 12 Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["c0c083ab-909a-4509-88ee-1af9eb74d842"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that right triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper W\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>U</mi>\n\t<mi>V</mi>\n\t<mi>W</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>. It's given that the side lengths of the right triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"upper R upper S equals 20\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper S upper T equals 48\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t\t<mi>T</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>48</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper T upper R equals 52\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn></math>. Corresponding angles in similar triangles are equal. It follows that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>.&nbsp;The hypotenuse of a right triangle is the longest side. It follows that the hypotenuse of triangle&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is side <math alttext=\"upper T upper R\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. The hypotenuse of a right triangle is the side opposite the right angle. Therefore, angle <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> is a right angle. The adjacent side of an acute angle in a right triangle is the side closest to the angle that is not the hypotenuse. It follows that the adjacent side of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is side <math alttext=\"upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The opposite side of an acute angle in a right triangle is the side across from the acute angle. It follows that the opposite side of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is side <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The tangent of an acute angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side. Therefore, <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals StartFraction upper R upper S Over upper S upper T EndFraction\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> in this equation yields <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals StartFraction 20 Over 48 EndFraction\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>48</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals five twelfths\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>. The tangents of two acute angles with equal measures are equal. Since the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>, it follows that <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals tangent upper W\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"tangent upper T\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi></math> in this equation yields <math alttext=\"five twelfths equals tangent upper W\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"tangent upper W\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"sine upper W\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"cosine upper W\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over tangent upper W EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959840,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"c9931030","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1691007959840,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"84b26634-2244-45e6-8504-ea367a0f2049","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"8c9abab8-de69-4713-93d3-c72423171dc9","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["c0c083ab-909a-4509-88ee-1af9eb74d842"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that right triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper W\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>U</mi>\n\t<mi>V</mi>\n\t<mi>W</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>. It's given that the side lengths of the right triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"upper R upper S equals 20\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper S upper T equals 48\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t\t<mi>T</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>48</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper T upper R equals 52\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn></math>. Corresponding angles in similar triangles are equal. It follows that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>.&nbsp;The hypotenuse of a right triangle is the longest side. It follows that the hypotenuse of triangle&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is side <math alttext=\"upper T upper R\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. The hypotenuse of a right triangle is the side opposite the right angle. Therefore, angle <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> is a right angle. The adjacent side of an acute angle in a right triangle is the side closest to the angle that is not the hypotenuse. It follows that the adjacent side of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is side <math alttext=\"upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The opposite side of an acute angle in a right triangle is the side across from the acute angle. It follows that the opposite side of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is side <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The tangent of an acute angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side. Therefore, <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals StartFraction upper R upper S Over upper S upper T EndFraction\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> in this equation yields <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals StartFraction 20 Over 48 EndFraction\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>48</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals five twelfths\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>. The tangents of two acute angles with equal measures are equal. Since the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>, it follows that <math alttext=\"tangent upper T equals tangent upper W\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"tangent upper T\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>T</mi></math> in this equation yields <math alttext=\"five twelfths equals tangent upper W\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"tangent upper W\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"five twelfths\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"sine upper W\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"cosine upper W\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over tangent upper W EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"upper R upper S equals 20\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"upper S upper T equals 48\"><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"upper T upper R equals 52\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p>The side lengths of right triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> are given. Triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper W\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>W</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper W\"><mi>W</mi>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"tangent upper W\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>W</mi></math>?</p>","externalid":"84b26634-2244-45e6-8504-ea367a0f2049","templateid":"1d70b3d9-2416-487b-98a3-5b949c8b5333","vaultid":"665adb83-0ed4-4f1b-baa1-36b2ef92be0d","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"92a1ef8c-7060-4466-9fa8-27745e2ac4d6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"five t