</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">For the right triangle shown, <math alttext="a equals 4"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and <math alttext="b equals 5"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>. Which expression represents the value of <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ce9a7bcd-0183-4f62-a1bb-3964274526f8","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"4 plus 5\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"8b2ae7f0-71b0-440d-b272-f50a2cc93ddf","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"StartRoot left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 5 right parenthesis EndRoot\"><msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math></p>"},{"id":"55f90e30-1ba5-430a-bf1d-d665410ef65f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"StartRoot 4 plus 5 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></math></p>"},{"id":"9eb1a5d4-3e6c-47b9-9abb-83efd0de607a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"StartRoot 4 squared plus 5 squared EndRoot\"><msqrt><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9eb1a5d4-3e6c-47b9-9abb-83efd0de607a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. By the Pythagorean theorem, if a right triangle has a hypotenuse with length <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> and legs with lengths <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>, then <math alttext="c squared equals a squared plus b squared"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. In the right triangle shown, the hypotenuse has length <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> and the legs have lengths <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>. It's given that <math alttext="a equals 4"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math alttext="b equals 5"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the Pythagorean theorem yields <math alttext="c squared equals 4 squared plus 5 squared"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="c equals plus or minus StartRoot 4 squared plus 5 squared EndRoot"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math>. Since the length of a side of a triangle must be positive, the value of <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="StartRoot 4 squared plus 5 squared EndRoot"><msqrt><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c9f8d1e9","external_id":"5466f88b-12d1-4e2d-a8ae-304ba95ffcae","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"9d1f2f37-92c8-47fc-9067-6389ba558a72","uId":"bc979c74-87d2-4dfa-a584-4ba351d97752","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"250.0pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 250.0 210.0\" height=\"210.0pt\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A right triangle. Refer to long description.\">\n  <g>\n    <g><defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 197.568  L 244.8 197.568  L 244.8 0  L 0 0  z \" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 190.368  L 237.6 190.368  L 237.6 7.2  L 7.2 7.2  z \" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <!-- $a$ -->\n    <defs>\n     <path d=\"M 46.296875 11.09375  L 47.59375 10  Q 42 3.203125 39.34375 1.09375  Q 36.703125 -1 33.703125 -1  Q 29.703125 -1 29.703125 3.09375  Q 29.703125 5.59375 32 14.59375  Q 26.40625 6.203125 21.703125 2.546875  Q 17 -1.09375 11.703125 -1.09375  Q 7.296875 -1.09375 4.5 1.953125  Q 1.703125 5 1.703125 10.5  Q 1.703125 18.09375 6.046875 26  Q 10.40625 33.90625 17.09375 39  Q 23.796875 44.09375 30.296875 44.09375  Q 37 44.09375 38.296875 38.296875  L 39.40625 43.09375  L 39.703125 43.40625  L 45.79