</math>, of a right circular cylinder is given by the formula <math alttext="upper V equals pi r squared h"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math alttext="pi r squared"><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is the area of the base of the cylinder and <math alttext="h"><mi>h</mi>
