	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="18 equals h"><mrow>
	<mn>18</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>h</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the height of the cylinder, in centimeters, is <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the area of the base, in square centimeters, not the height, in centimeters, of the cylinder.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the height, in centimeters, of a cylinder if its volume is <math alttext="432"><mn>432</mn>
</math> cubic centimeters and the area of its base is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math>, cubic centimeters.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the height, in centimeters, of a cylinder if its volume is <math alttext="432"><mn>432</mn>
</math> cubic centimeters and the area of its base is <math alttext="one twenty fourth"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math>, cubic centimeters.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"cecbdeba","external_id":"d0ab21dc-5c27-4da2-a45b-fa400982d6bc","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e0d2b69d-4ff2-49ac-8117-0d62a4d46fd6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right circular cylinder has a volume of <math alttext=\"432\"><mn>432</mn>\n</math> cubic centimeters. The area of the base of the cylinder is <math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math> square centimeters. What is the height, in centimeters, of the cylinder?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"a1a3902c-ae97-4535-89ca-ff041a9f6877","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1cb54675-ee87-444c-833b-542df527f557","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0f154f37-ccd2-42f4-9d49-8d385ad8f85c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"216\"><mn>216</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8e1d20fb-ef97-4a89-a290-4b25fa22a7e7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10,368\"><mn>10,368</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["a1a3902c-ae97-4535-89ca-ff041a9f6877"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The volume, <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math>, of a right circular cylinder is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper V equals pi r squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"pi r squared\"><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is the area of the base of the cylinder and <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> is the height. It&rsquo;s given that a right circular cylinder has a volume of <math alttext=\"432\"><mn>432</mn>\n</math> cubic centimeters and the area of the bas