<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for diagram of 3 lines" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled, c, s, and t.</li>
<li>Line c intersects both line s and line t.</li>
<li>At the intersection of line c and line s, 1 angle is labeled clockwise from top left as follows:
<ul>
<li>Top right: x°</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>At the intersection of line c and line t, 1 angle is labeled clockwise from top left as follows:
<ul>
<li>Top left: 110°</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the figure shown, line <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> intersects parallel lines <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["70"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["70"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math>. Based on the figure, the angle with measure&nbsp;<math alttext="110 degree"><mn>110</mn><mo>°</mo></math> and the angle vertical to the angle with measure&nbsp;<math alttext="x degree"><mi>x</mi><mo>°</mo></math> are same side interior angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, the angle vertical to the angle with measure&nbsp;<math alttext="x degree"><mi>x</mi><mo>°</mo></math> also has measure <math alttext="x degree"><mi>x</mi><mo>°</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that lines <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> are parallel. Therefore, same side interior angles between lines <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> are supplementary. It follows that <math alttext="x plus 110 equals 180"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>110</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>180</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="110"><mn>110</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="x equals 70"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>70</mn>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"cf0d3050","external_id":"b09e0918-6dfc-4b50-b503-bbdd89fe3480","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"29301565-33b3-4f24-9430-2e14f3057510","uId":"a80b022b-78dc-4c0b-a2cb-71fe0e04a189","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"209.17206pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 190.75562 209.17206\" width=\"190.75562pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A diagram of 3 lines. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 209.17206 \nL 190.75562 209.17206 \nL 190.75562 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p20a793853b)\" d=\"M 7.2 62.068295 \nL 166.23 62.068295 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:0.5;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p20a793853b)\" d=\"M 7.2 117.050114 \nL 166.23 117.050114 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:0.5;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_3\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p20a793853b)\" d=\"M 14.809091 172.031932 \nL 166.990909 20.831932 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:0.5;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <!-- $\\itc$ -->\n    <defs>\n     <path d=\"M 35 10.703125 \nL 36.59375 9.703125 \nQ 32 3.90