</math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The graph of the given equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane is a circle. What is the length of the radius of this circle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"8a608016-859b-44e1-9cdc-28dbadd6cf5b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b761b318-f332-44bc-94a6-890c930ef1aa","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c30810c6-45d1-47ce-b982-dd308f951f94","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"474ab7b4-a22e-4ea2-86ca-d8daf087b11b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c30810c6-45d1-47ce-b982-dd308f951f94"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>. The graph of the given equation,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 81"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn></math>, is a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane. This equation can be written as&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 9 squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h equals 6"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k equals 3"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r equals 9"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Therefore, the radius of this circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-coordinate of the center, not the radius, of the circle defined by the given equation.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the center, not the radius, of the circle defined by the given equation.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of the radius squared, not the radius, of the circle defined by the given equation.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"d03e29f1","external_id":"5235bd99-6451-4d06-9e8e-2810669a0c43","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b4c8cf08-87b3-4e01-91bc-ecbfa39ec1e1","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 3 right parenthesis squared equals 81\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>81</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the given equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane is a circle. What is the length of the radius of this circle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8a608016-859b-44e1-9cdc-28dbadd6cf5b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b761b318-f332-44bc-94a6-890c930ef1aa","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c30810c6-45d1-47ce-b982-dd308f951f94","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"474ab7b4-a22e-4ea2-86ca-d8daf087b11b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["c30810c6-45d1-47ce-b982-dd308f951f94"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The e