</math> and <math alttext="upper S upper T upper U"><mrow>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
	<mi>U</mi>
</mrow>
</math> are similar, where <math alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi>
</math> corresponds to <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math>. If the measure of angle <math alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="18 degree"><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure of angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"03776955-2c92-4304-863f-acf9c346b180","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18 degree\"><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"50c085b5-b8fa-4b4a-9898-9cc1e3072019","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mrow><mn>72</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"5f4780ed-26aa-400d-93cf-c55abf1a637f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"82 degree\"><mrow><mn>82</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"6272610f-d7a8-439a-a020-45c169c82d4a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"162 degree\"><mrow><mn>162</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["50c085b5-b8fa-4b4a-9898-9cc1e3072019"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. In similar triangles, corresponding angles are congruent. It&rsquo;s given that right triangles <math alttext="upper P upper Q upper R"><mrow>
	<mi>P</mi>
	<mi>Q</mi>
	<mi>R</mi>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="upper S upper T upper U"><mrow>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
	<mi>U</mi>
</mrow>
</math> are similar, where angle <math alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi>
</math> corresponds to angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math>. It follows that angle <math alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi>
</math> is congruent to angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math>. In the triangles shown, angle <math alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi>
</math> and angle <math alttext="upper U"><mi>U</mi>
</math> are both marked as right angles, so angle <math alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi>
</math> and angle <math alttext="upper U"><mi>U</mi>
</math> are corresponding angles. It follows that angle <math alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi>
</math> and angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> are corresponding angles, and thus, angle <math alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi>
</math> is congruent to angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of angle <math alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="18 degree"><mn>18</mn><mo>°</mo></math>, so the measure of angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math> is also <math alttext="18 degree"><mn>18</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Angle <math alttext="upper U"><mi>U</mi>
</math> is a right angle, so the measure of angle <math alttext="upper U"><mi>U</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="90 degree"><mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext="180 degree"><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Thus, the sum of the measures of the interior angles of triangle <math alttext="upper S upper T upper U"><mrow>
	<mi>S</mi>
	<mi>T</mi>
	<mi>U</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is <math alttext="180"><mn>180</mn>
</math> degrees. Let <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> represent the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math>. It follows that <math alttext="s plus 18 plus 90 equals 180"><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>, or <math alttext="s plus 108 equals 180"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>s</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>108</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>180</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="108"><mn>108</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="s equals 72"><mrow>
	<mi>s</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>72</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, if the measure of angle <math alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math> degrees, then the measure of angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="72"><mn>72</mn>
</math> degrees.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <math alttext="upper T"><mi>T</mi>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angle <math alttext="upper S"><mi>S</mi>
</math> and angle <math alttext="upper U"><mi>U</mi>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"d5f349b7","external_id":"dbae1ccb-c727-453d-aad3-d9808097dcfd","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"09f06f5b-3c03-4696-8e64-99a9f13891e4","uId":"16b8a398-2d02-400e-b5e3-f1270f5a9c35","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"344.657\" height=\"179.856\" viewBox=\"0 0 344.657 179.856\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Right triangles upper P upper Q upper R and upper S upper T upper U. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"f01edb93-fd70-4b41-a23f-15a73e843f4c\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><polygon points=\"166.272 18.894 166.272 120.846 15.862 120.846 166.272 18.894\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><polygon points=\"326.922 54.937 326.922 120.846 229.687 120.846 326.922 54.937\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><rect x=\"154.932\" y=\"109.506\" width=\"11.34\" height=\"11.34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></rect><rect x=\"315.582\" y=\"109.506\" width=\"11.34\" height=\"11.34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></rect><path d=\"M7.19,122.81a3.579,3.579,0,0,1,2.209.843,2.6,2.6,0,0,1,1.085,2.141,3.669,3.669,0,0,1-1.366,2.859A4.48,4.48,0,0,1,6.1,129.845a4.031,4.031,0,0,1-1.356-.175.806.806,0,0,1-.039-.193.42.42,0,0,1,.116-.31,3.346,3.346,0,0,0,.466.039,3.631,3.631,0,0,0,2.432-.97,3.36,3.36,0,0,0,1.114-2.674,1.825,1.825,0,0,0-2.093-2.035,5.317,5.317,0,0,0-1.211.087c-.2.058-.314.158-.34.3