 alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>P</mi>\n\t<mi>Q</mi>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper S upper T upper U\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n\t<mi>U</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are similar, where <math alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi>\n</math> corresponds to <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math>. If the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper Q\"><mi>Q</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"18 degree\"><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math>?</p>","externalid":"dbae1ccb-c727-453d-aad3-d9808097dcfd","templateid":"cf4bf252-f5c4-4081-a1be-3a7ec602a618","vaultid":"09f06f5b-3c03-4696-8e64-99a9f13891e4","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"03776955-2c92-4304-863f-acf9c346b180","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18 degree\"><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"50c085b5-b8fa-4b4a-9898-9cc1e3072019","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mrow><mn>72</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"5f4780ed-26aa-400d-93cf-c55abf1a637f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"82 degree\"><mrow><mn>82</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"6272610f-d7a8-439a-a020-45c169c82d4a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"162 degree\"><mrow><mn>162</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959837,"updateDate":1691007959837}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959837, 1691007959837),
    ($SATQ$d621cffb$SATQ$, $SATQ$b7b7672e-ce42-4e19-9094-c2ba6966c496$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A sphere has a radius of <math alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 5 EndFraction"><mfrac>
	<mn>17</mn>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mfrac>
</math> feet. What is the volume, in cubic feet, of the sphere?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"cf6fea3f-5f33-490a-92a7-983247e3672a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 5 pi Over 17 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mn>17</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3aa46ca4-b38e-4dc8-9c5a-aa2610f7b6e6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 68 pi Over 15 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>68</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"942c50a1-a037-40a1-ad56-978b438a0ee2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 32 pi Over 5 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>32</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8b16e1db-9b5b-4f23-9386-e5d8bd020228","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 19,652 pi Over 375 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>19,652</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>&pi;</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mn>375</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8b16e1db-9b5b-4f23-9386-e5d8bd020228"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. The volume, <math alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi>
</math>, of a sphere can be found using the formula <math alttext="upper V equals four thirds pi r cubed"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, where <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> is the radius of the sphere. It&rsquo;s given that the sphere has a radius of <math alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 5 EndFraction"><mfrac>
	<mn>17</mn>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mfrac>
</math> feet. Substituting <math alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 5 EndFraction"><mfrac>
	<mn>17</mn>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mfrac>
</math> for <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
